# nyxloom provider secrets — TEMPLATE. Copy to `secrets.env` (gitignored) and fill in:
#     cp secrets.env.example secrets.env    # then edit secrets.env, then restart nyxloomd
#
# `secrets.env` is loaded into the nyxloomd daemon as a second docker env_file
# (alongside .env). NEVER commit real values.
#
# Consumers (least-privilege — who actually needs each key):
#   AA_API_KEY          the DAEMON itself: benchmark fetch (ArtificialAnalysisSource,
#                       https://artificialanalysis.ai/api/v2). NOT forwarded to any CLI.
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY  opencode / reasonix CLI runs (OpenRouter free + paid routes).
#   DEEPSEEK_API_KEY    opencode / reasonix CLI runs (deepseek-v4 implementer routes).
#
# Claude and codex authenticate via manual subscription plans — NO API key here.
#
# Key delivery to the CLIs (CR-13a, 2026-08-03 — this paragraph previously
# described the fork+exec inheritance model, which is no longer what happens):
# a CLI receives ONLY the env vars its route's `secrets = [...]` names in
# routes.toml, plus a short non-authority operational allowlist (PATH, HOME,
# LANG, proxy vars — see containment.BASE_ENV_ALLOW) and the attempt's own
# identity. There is no inheritance and no denylist. A key added to this file
# reaches nothing until a route asks for it by name, so AA_API_KEY is not
# forwarded to any CLI because no route declares it — not because it is on a
# list somewhere.
#
# An UNTRUSTED route (every free endpoint, and anything that does not declare
# `trust = "operator"`) additionally runs in a per-use container: the declared
# names are the only ones that cross the boundary, passed as `-e NAME` so no
# secret VALUE ever appears in an argv or in a serialized spec.json.

# ================== services requiring API keys ==================

# https://artificialanalysis.ai/
AA_API_KEY=

# ================== Model providers requiring API keys ===========

# https://openrouter.ai/
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# https://platform.deepseek.com/
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
